# AI Autopilot Control Center

This is the always-on operating plan for MedSpa Growth Engine. It explains how the system keeps working after the owner completes the required setup: sourcing leads, researching them, drafting specific outreach, following up, preparing calls, supporting delivery, monitoring clients, and escalating only when human judgment is needed.

## Autopilot Principle

The system should feel like an operator, not a tool.

It should:

- Keep finding new medspa leads.
- Research each lead before outreach.
- Identify the most likely pain point.
- Draft specific messages around that pain.
- Follow up on time.
- Triage replies.
- Prepare the owner for sales calls.
- Create delivery tasks after a close.
- Monitor live clients.
- Prepare weekly updates and churn-risk alerts.

It should not:

- Blast generic outreach.
- Invent pain points.
- Ignore opt-outs.
- Make medical, legal, or revenue guarantees.
- Touch secrets without owner-controlled setup.
- Make final sales or client-trust decisions without the owner.

## Autopilot Levels

| Level | Name | What AI can do | Owner involvement |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | Manual Assist | Research, draft, summarize | Owner runs actions manually |
| 1 | Draft Autopilot | Build lead lists, research, write messages, queue follow-ups | Owner approves sends |
| 2 | Controlled Send | Send approved sequences within daily limits, stop on replies/opt-outs | Owner reviews daily brief and hot replies |
| 3 | Sales Assist | Triage replies, book-call prompts, call briefs, recaps, proposal drafts | Owner takes calls and approves offers |
| 4 | Delivery Assist | Build delivery boards, check blockers, draft client updates | Owner handles credentials and go-live |
| 5 | Retention Monitor | Weekly reports, error checks, churn-risk alerts, upsell timing | Owner handles save calls and strategic changes |

Default launch mode:

**Level 1 until inboxes, compliance rules, sending limits, unsubscribe handling, and lead quality are proven.**

Move to Level 2 only after:

- The first campaign has been reviewed.
- Messages are specific and safe.
- Bounce/opt-out handling works.
- Daily send limits are set.
- The owner can review the daily brief.

## Always-On Schedule

| Time/Cadence | Autopilot action | Output |
|---|---|---|
| Daily morning | Build owner brief | Hot replies, calls, follow-ups, blockers, highest-value action |
| Daily | Source leads from selected markets | New leads with source and status |
| Daily | Enrich priority leads | Research brief, pain hypothesis, fit score |
| Daily | Draft or send due outreach | Outreach log and next follow-up dates |
| Daily | Triage replies | Classification, suggested response, owner-needed flag |
| Daily | Monitor delivery blockers | Missing access, overdue tasks, QA issues |
| Weekly | Review pipeline metrics | Leads, sends, replies, calls, proposals, closes |
| Weekly | Review client health | Reports sent, workflow errors, churn risks |
| Monthly | Improve offer and campaigns | Winning hooks, weak messages, retention ideas |

## Owner Handoff Triggers

The AI should notify the owner when:

- A lead asks for pricing.
- A lead asks to book a call.
- A lead replies with a strong pain signal.
- A lead objects in a way that needs trust.
- A prospect complains or asks to stop contact.
- A proposal needs final terms.
- A client has missing access for more than 48 hours.
- A client workflow has repeated errors.
- A client shows churn risk.
- A paid ad needs approval or spend changes.

## Lead Quality Gate

No lead moves into outreach unless it has:

- Clinic name.
- Location.
- Website or social profile.
- Contact route.
- Service category.
- At least one real observation from website, reviews, social, booking path, or ads.
- A suspected revenue leak.
- Fit score.
- Recommended first-touch angle.

If any of these are missing, status stays:

`Research Needed`

## Outreach Quality Gate

No message is approved unless it passes all checks:

- It references a real observation.
- It names one likely business pain.
- It connects that pain to the Lost Revenue Recovery OS.
- It is short enough to read fast.
- It has one clear next step.
- It does not sound like a mass template.
- It does not guarantee results.
- It includes opt-out handling where required.

Bad message:

> We help medspas automate their business with AI. Are you free for a call?

Good message:

> I saw you push consultations from Instagram into a booking link, but there is no obvious follow-up path for people who do not book right away. We install a recovery layer for medspas so missed consults, no-shows, and lapsed clients get followed up consistently. Worth me sending the 4-leak map?

## Daily Owner Brief Standard

The owner should see one compact brief every day:

```text
Date:
Money action today:
Hot replies:
Calls today:
Follow-ups due:
New researched leads:
Messages waiting approval:
Delivery/client blockers:
Client risks:
AI completed:
Owner needed:
```

## Monitoring Rules

The autopilot should keep these queues clean:

- Leads without research older than 24 hours.
- Approved leads without first touch.
- Contacted leads without next follow-up date.
- Replies without classification.
- Calls without call brief.
- Proposals without next follow-up.
- Clients with missing access.
- Live clients without weekly report.
- Workflow errors without owner alert.

## Autopilot Safety

The system can be aggressive with work ethic, not reckless with trust.

Required safeguards:

- Daily send limits.
- Bounce tracking.
- Unsubscribe/stop-contact handling.
- No patient data in prompts.
- No scraping behind logins without permission.
- No bypassing platform terms.
- No public storage of secrets or private client links.
- Human approval for new campaigns, paid ads, pricing, contracts, complaints, and go-live.

## What The Owner Completes

The owner must provide:

- Sending email account.
- Domain/inbox setup.
- Calendar booking link.
- Outreach compliance preference.
- Target cities or markets.
- Approved daily send limit.
- Approved offer/pricing.
- Payment link or invoice process.
- Client contract or engagement letter.
- Access to n8n/Make/Zapier/Sheets if automation will run live.

After that, the AI operator can run the day-to-day system and escalate only when needed.
